{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":680986,"ns":0,"title":"Aporia","extract":"In philosophy, an aporia (Ancient Greek: ᾰ̓πορῐ́ᾱ, romanized: aporíā, lit. '\"lacking passage\", also: \"impasse\", \"difficulty in passage\", \"puzzlement\"') is a conundrum or state of puzzlement. In rhetoric, it is a declaration of doubt, made for rhetorical purpose and often feigned.","description":"State of puzzlement or expression of doubt, in philosophy and rhetoric","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}